        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the following quantities:\n- Total computers: 20\n- Unfixable computers: 20% of 20\n- Computers needing spare parts: 40% of 20\n\nI needed to find out how many computers John was able to fix right away. To solve this, I first calculated the number of unfixable computers:\n20% of 20 = 0.20 * 20 = 4 computers\n\nNext, I calculated the number of computers needing spare parts:\n40% of 20 = 0.40 * 20 = 8 computers\n\nTo find the number of computers John was able to fix right away, I subtracted the unfixable and those needing spare parts from the total:\n20 - 4 - 8 = 8 computers\n\nI checked this result by confirming that the sum of the unfixable, those needing spare parts, and those fixed right away equals the total number of computers:\n4 (unfixable) + 8 (needing spare parts) + 8 (fixed right away) = 20\n\nThis check verified that my solution was correct. The operation I would reuse is calculating percentages of a total and then performing subtraction to find the remaining quantity. This is useful in similar problems involving distribution and remaining quantities.\n\nFINAL: 8",
