        "target": "Five months ago, Fred earned $1000. Mike earned 10 times more than Fred, so Mike's salary five months ago was 10 * $1000 = $10000. Mike's salary has increased by 40 percent since then. To find the new salary, we calculate 40% of $10000, which is 0.40 * $10000 = $4000. Adding this to his original salary, Mike's current salary is $10000 + $4000 = $14000.\n\nFINAL: 14000",
